1
00:00:00,033 --> 00:00:01,418
(This drama complied with production
guidelines for filming child actors,)

2
00:00:01,501 --> 00:00:02,936
(and some scenes used
generative AI technology.)

3
00:00:03,103 --> 00:00:04,621
(Episode 28)

4
00:00:04,704 --> 00:00:06,373
Mom!

5
00:00:07,674 --> 00:00:09,376
Mom!

6
00:00:12,712 --> 00:00:13,847
Mom?

7
00:00:16,049 --> 00:00:17,283
What is this?

8
00:00:19,019 --> 00:00:21,955
Seriously? Did she stay out again?

9
00:00:37,137 --> 00:00:39,406
What?

10
00:00:42,976 --> 00:00:47,180
Jung A, my mom isn't home.

11
00:00:48,415 --> 00:00:50,183
She left her phone behind, too.

12
00:00:50,583 --> 00:00:53,253
- She's fighting fire with fire.
- Fire with fire?

13
00:00:53,420 --> 00:00:55,622
You rebelled, so she's rebelling back.

14
00:00:56,056 --> 00:00:59,092
- She's really angry.
- You think so?

15
00:01:01,995 --> 00:01:03,296
Yes.

16
00:01:12,705 --> 00:01:16,910
The seal. The company seal...

17
00:01:50,343 --> 00:01:52,812
This can't be happening.

18
00:01:53,146 --> 00:01:55,882
(Your current balance is zero dollars,
and your available funds are zero.)

19
00:02:03,256 --> 00:02:05,291
My phone...

20
00:02:07,293 --> 00:02:09,662
Where's my phone...

21
00:02:15,135 --> 00:02:16,836
Honey...

22
00:02:17,770 --> 00:02:19,706
Honey, what do I do?

23
00:02:20,673 --> 00:02:22,509
Nothing bad will happen, right?

24
00:02:33,553 --> 00:02:34,687
Mom!

25
00:02:35,255 --> 00:02:37,757
I said if you stayed out all night,
so would I.

26
00:02:38,091 --> 00:02:39,692
Are you really doing this?

27
00:02:41,161 --> 00:02:42,879
And you left your phone behind...

28
00:02:42,962 --> 00:02:44,831
Where were you?

29
00:02:48,501 --> 00:02:49,936
Ji Ni.

30
00:02:51,504 --> 00:02:53,206
What is it now?

31
00:02:55,008 --> 00:02:56,676
I...

32
00:02:57,510 --> 00:03:00,713
I think I've been scammed.

33
00:03:02,215 --> 00:03:04,517
What are you saying? Scammed?

34
00:03:05,952 --> 00:03:07,554
Indonesia...

35
00:03:07,687 --> 00:03:08,821
That deal was a scam?

36
00:03:09,189 --> 00:03:13,693
I don't know yet, but the lawyer
won't answer his phone.

37
00:03:14,227 --> 00:03:17,297
The company balance is zero.

38
00:03:18,765 --> 00:03:20,700
- Zero?
- Yes.

39
00:03:21,334 --> 00:03:24,404
I went to the office.
I thought maybe I'd misread something...

40
00:03:24,737 --> 00:03:26,206
- But then...
- But then?

41
00:03:28,841 --> 00:03:31,311
The company seal is gone too.

42
00:03:34,547 --> 00:03:36,282
What do we do?

43
00:03:36,449 --> 00:03:37,984
I'm so frightened.

44
00:03:38,952 --> 00:03:41,554
I put everything into it.
What do I do, Ji Ni?

45
00:03:42,622 --> 00:03:43,623
It's still...

46
00:03:44,791 --> 00:03:47,627
Nothing is confirmed yet.

47
00:03:48,294 --> 00:03:50,096
He's not that kind of man.

48
00:03:50,897 --> 00:03:55,101
He's been with us since your dad's time,
so I trusted him completely.

49
00:03:56,469 --> 00:03:59,772
If this goes wrong, we're finished.

50
00:04:01,174 --> 00:04:02,775
That won't happen, Mom.

51
00:04:02,942 --> 00:04:04,410
Just calm down.

52
00:04:06,212 --> 00:04:07,780
Hold on a second...

53
00:04:25,398 --> 00:04:29,636
The number you have dialed does not exist.
Please check the number...

54
00:04:30,970 --> 00:04:33,740
This is driving me crazy!

55
00:04:39,712 --> 00:04:41,247
Hello, Ms. Kim.

56
00:04:41,781 --> 00:04:44,951
Yes, I called you several times yesterday.

57
00:04:45,351 --> 00:04:50,623
Ms. Kim, I can't reach the lawyer
I'd been working with.

58
00:04:50,857 --> 00:04:55,328
And the bank balance looks strange.

59
00:04:55,628 --> 00:04:58,715
Could you ask your husband for me?

60
00:04:58,798 --> 00:05:01,701
What should I do in a case like this?

61
00:05:02,602 --> 00:05:04,604
Yes.

62
00:05:05,605 --> 00:05:08,775
Yes, thank you.

63
00:05:09,842 --> 00:05:11,210
Who was that?

64
00:05:11,577 --> 00:05:14,514
Ms. Kim.

65
00:05:14,947 --> 00:05:17,216
Her husband runs a business.

66
00:05:18,751 --> 00:05:21,187
Eat some porridge first.
You haven't had a thing.

67
00:05:21,554 --> 00:05:24,157
Yes. My stomach already hurts.

68
00:05:25,625 --> 00:05:28,612
I told you business isn't for everyone.

69
00:05:28,695 --> 00:05:32,999
Your dad set it all up,
so I thought I just had to stamp things.

70
00:05:33,833 --> 00:05:35,735
Aren't you going to work?

71
00:05:36,736 --> 00:05:39,072
Will you be all right alone?
Want me to be with you?

72
00:05:39,205 --> 00:05:40,573
No need.

73
00:05:40,773 --> 00:05:43,076
You can't keep missing work. Go on.

74
00:05:43,676 --> 00:05:47,013
All right. Call me if anything happens.

75
00:05:51,351 --> 00:05:54,654
Dad, it's nothing serious, right?

76
00:05:55,555 --> 00:05:57,056
Please help us.

77
00:05:57,724 --> 00:06:01,527
Without you, every day feels anxious.

78
00:06:08,568 --> 00:06:10,636
Sun Kyung, why haven't you eaten?

79
00:06:11,371 --> 00:06:12,956
I have no appetite.

80
00:06:13,039 --> 00:06:15,241
No appetite, my foot.
Her high school reunion is tomorrow.

81
00:06:15,341 --> 00:06:17,677
The dress I was going to wear doesn't fit.

82
00:06:18,144 --> 00:06:19,846
I'll have to skip meals today.

83
00:06:21,314 --> 00:06:22,849
That dress was already tight
when you bought it.

84
00:06:22,949 --> 00:06:25,118
It was the only size left.
What else could I do?

85
00:06:25,284 --> 00:06:26,719
I'll just have to fit into it.

86
00:06:26,819 --> 00:06:28,305
Don't push yourself.

87
00:06:28,388 --> 00:06:30,723
You're lovely as you are without a diet.

88
00:06:30,857 --> 00:06:32,592
Thank you, Sa Bin.

89
00:06:32,692 --> 00:06:34,927
So you're going to show off a dress.

90
00:06:35,695 --> 00:06:38,097
We don't gather to drink as men do.

91
00:06:38,197 --> 00:06:41,100
Stop spending so much.
Every reunion leaves the account empty.

92
00:06:41,234 --> 00:06:42,735
You'd think you were building a school.

93
00:06:42,835 --> 00:06:44,704
What would I live for without that fun?

94
00:06:45,071 --> 00:06:47,140
You went to Ilyeong Girls' High School,
didn't you, Sun Kyung?

95
00:06:47,407 --> 00:06:50,843
- Do you know No Yeong Ju?
- No Yeong Ju?

96
00:06:51,244 --> 00:06:52,712
Is she from the 36th graduating class?

97
00:06:52,812 --> 00:06:57,283
I'm not sure which class,
but she's your age, so the 36th?

98
00:06:57,850 --> 00:06:59,852
The name does sound familiar...

99
00:07:00,787 --> 00:07:04,891
The one in the broadcasting club
who could really sing...

100
00:07:05,925 --> 00:07:08,594
You do know her.
Yes, she mentioned the broadcasting club.

101
00:07:08,694 --> 00:07:11,798
But if she doesn't come to the reunions,
I don't know much about her.

102
00:07:11,931 --> 00:07:14,700
She probably didn't stand out
the way you did.

103
00:07:14,834 --> 00:07:16,702
That was 30 years ago.

104
00:07:16,869 --> 00:07:19,205
How do you know No Yeong Ju, though?

105
00:07:19,605 --> 00:07:22,608
She's a patient at my clinic.

106
00:07:22,809 --> 00:07:24,677
Does your clinic take resumes
before handing out medicine?

107
00:07:25,011 --> 00:07:27,364
- You know her high school? That's close.
- Father.

108
00:07:27,447 --> 00:07:32,251
At a clinic, we don't call it close.
We call it a regular, General.

109
00:07:32,351 --> 00:07:33,953
A regular.

110
00:07:34,187 --> 00:07:35,555
Well, that makes sense.

111
00:07:43,629 --> 00:07:46,098
Can't you read the room for once?

112
00:07:46,666 --> 00:07:49,419
Your dad already reads into everything,

113
00:07:49,502 --> 00:07:52,505
so keep quiet unless you
want him grilling me about this.

114
00:07:52,805 --> 00:07:54,540
If this annoys me, I'll move out again.

115
00:07:54,674 --> 00:07:56,576
- It's not like I have no home.
- Or no building?

116
00:07:57,243 --> 00:07:58,678
Look at the landlord!

117
00:07:58,911 --> 00:08:00,246
Don't get cocky!

118
00:08:00,546 --> 00:08:03,483
I have no interest in pairing you
with a grandmother.

119
00:08:03,616 --> 00:08:05,135
Does that make sense? She's my mom's age.

120
00:08:05,218 --> 00:08:09,021
If you'd married two years ago,
she'd be a grandmother too.

121
00:08:09,288 --> 00:08:11,891
- What's so bad about being a grandma?
- "What's so bad?"

122
00:08:12,658 --> 00:08:15,461
This is why I have to suspect you.
What's with that reaction?

123
00:08:15,561 --> 00:08:20,333
I just don't want a regular patient
of mine caught up in silly suspicion.

124
00:08:20,700 --> 00:08:22,335
I don't buy that.

125
00:08:22,668 --> 00:08:24,053
You said she sings well, too.

126
00:08:24,136 --> 00:08:26,272
You have a weakness for good singers.

127
00:08:26,973 --> 00:08:28,541
That's true.

128
00:08:29,609 --> 00:08:31,477
Does she know you're tone-deaf?

129
00:08:31,744 --> 00:08:34,280
- She'd be disappointed if she knew.
- She isn't.

130
00:08:35,281 --> 00:08:37,183
She said she'd be glad I'm not stone-deaf.

131
00:08:37,350 --> 00:08:38,784
Stone-deaf?

132
00:08:40,186 --> 00:08:43,289
Stone-deaf. She must be quite a woman.

133
00:08:44,957 --> 00:08:46,492
My dear nephew.

134
00:08:46,692 --> 00:08:49,495
That's the caliber of people I meet.

135
00:08:49,929 --> 00:08:52,598
Now that you know, would you please go?

136
00:08:53,065 --> 00:08:55,034
Suspicious.

137
00:08:55,601 --> 00:08:56,802
Very suspicious.

138
00:08:57,169 --> 00:09:00,239
Suspicious? What am I, a spy?

139
00:09:07,280 --> 00:09:12,985
<i>O sole mio</i>

140
00:09:49,855 --> 00:09:54,226
- Well done. Shall we take a break?
- Yes.

141
00:09:57,129 --> 00:10:02,702
Singing takes more energy than it seems,
so I brought snacks.

142
00:10:03,436 --> 00:10:04,737
What is that?

143
00:10:04,837 --> 00:10:08,674
It's like a Vietnamese savory pancake.
Please try some.

144
00:10:08,941 --> 00:10:11,377
Actually, my grandson just got discharged.

145
00:10:11,577 --> 00:10:13,730
- That's wonderful!
- Congratulations.

146
00:10:13,813 --> 00:10:15,314
Thank you for the food.

147
00:10:15,414 --> 00:10:17,216
Please enjoy.

148
00:10:19,852 --> 00:10:24,090
Thank you. It's all thanks
to everyone's support and concern.

149
00:10:24,490 --> 00:10:27,510
I missed so many classes,
and I felt terrible about it...

150
00:10:27,593 --> 00:10:31,797
I thought of bringing rice cakes,
but my daughter-in-law made these.

151
00:10:32,331 --> 00:10:35,451
My daughter-in-law is Vietnamese.

152
00:10:35,534 --> 00:10:37,603
So you arranged an international marriage?

153
00:10:39,005 --> 00:10:43,776
It wasn't planned.
Fate simply worked out that way.

154
00:10:44,176 --> 00:10:47,113
Her Korean is so good,
she runs circles around me.

155
00:10:49,849 --> 00:10:51,183
This is delicious.

156
00:10:51,484 --> 00:10:52,702
- So good.
- Really delicious.

157
00:10:52,785 --> 00:10:53,986
I've never tasted anything like it.

158
00:10:54,587 --> 00:10:55,788
She's a fine cook.

159
00:11:00,192 --> 00:11:03,596
I brought plenty, so take some home.

160
00:11:03,829 --> 00:11:06,866
My daughter-in-law is generous,
so she packed a huge amount.

161
00:11:07,133 --> 00:11:08,251
Thank you.

162
00:11:08,334 --> 00:11:09,468
I'll take some.

163
00:11:10,569 --> 00:11:13,856
May I take just one more?

164
00:11:13,939 --> 00:11:15,841
- Of course.
- It's so good.

165
00:11:16,809 --> 00:11:18,210
Such a good cook.

166
00:11:19,845 --> 00:11:22,381
- What's this?
- Open it at home.

167
00:11:23,983 --> 00:11:25,484
Thank you.

168
00:11:26,652 --> 00:11:28,354
Delicious.

169
00:11:34,493 --> 00:11:37,063
- So where's your mom?
- I don't know.

170
00:11:37,697 --> 00:11:39,932
Probably meeting one person after another.

171
00:11:40,633 --> 00:11:43,269
Jung A, it'll be fine, right?

172
00:11:43,803 --> 00:11:46,505
- Still no word from the lawyer?
- No.

173
00:11:47,273 --> 00:11:50,176
I told my mom it would be fine,
but...

174
00:11:50,509 --> 00:11:53,145
- I'm frightened too.
- You never get a calm day.

175
00:11:54,313 --> 00:11:56,182
This must be so hard on you.

176
00:11:56,449 --> 00:11:58,384
I know...

177
00:12:00,419 --> 00:12:02,321
Excuse me.

178
00:12:05,091 --> 00:12:06,158
Goodness!

179
00:12:07,460 --> 00:12:09,028
What brings you here?

180
00:12:09,128 --> 00:12:10,362
My studio is here.

181
00:12:10,496 --> 00:12:13,065
Right, Seung Woo mentioned that.

182
00:12:13,365 --> 00:12:16,219
Then the singing class you run...

183
00:12:16,302 --> 00:12:17,970
Yes, it's here.

184
00:12:18,971 --> 00:12:21,640
After the class, we had these.

185
00:12:21,841 --> 00:12:25,595
You refill my coffee so often,
so I brought some, give them a try.

186
00:12:25,678 --> 00:12:27,246
Thank you.

187
00:12:27,680 --> 00:12:29,381
Mai made them.

188
00:12:29,648 --> 00:12:32,151
To celebrate O Reum coming home.
So try them.

189
00:12:33,352 --> 00:12:34,487
Yes.

190
00:12:34,787 --> 00:12:38,424
Why the long face? Is something wrong?

191
00:12:43,629 --> 00:12:46,031
So she's O Reum's grandmother?

192
00:12:46,132 --> 00:12:48,567
The official wife? No way.

193
00:12:52,304 --> 00:12:56,642
Forget it. I don't have the energy
to get angry about that anymore.

194
00:12:56,876 --> 00:12:59,445
It really is a small world.

195
00:12:59,812 --> 00:13:01,480
You never know
who you'll cross paths with.

196
00:13:02,448 --> 00:13:04,683
I just hope nothing else happens.

197
00:13:04,817 --> 00:13:06,903
I can't even bring myself to draw.

198
00:13:06,986 --> 00:13:09,855
Of course. Your head must be a mess.

199
00:13:12,958 --> 00:13:17,280
My mom took even the shares
that her children held, so...

200
00:13:17,363 --> 00:13:20,399
If this collapses, it might truly be over.

201
00:13:20,633 --> 00:13:22,368
I'm going out of my mind.

202
00:13:24,170 --> 00:13:26,372
She's that handsome guy's mother?

203
00:13:26,739 --> 00:13:29,508
I can't believe it.
How old was she when she got married?

204
00:13:30,976 --> 00:13:33,512
I'd better marry soon
if I want a son like that...

205
00:13:33,746 --> 00:13:35,714
Get to work. I'm leaving.

206
00:13:36,148 --> 00:13:37,133
Ji Ni.

207
00:13:37,216 --> 00:13:39,084
Let me refill your coffee. Take it.

208
00:13:39,752 --> 00:13:40,753
No thanks.

209
00:13:47,426 --> 00:13:49,395
She looks so down.

210
00:13:57,169 --> 00:14:02,408
It seems my dad's company lawyer
vanished with the company's money.

211
00:14:03,475 --> 00:14:07,046
So my mom is completely
distraught right now.

212
00:14:08,914 --> 00:14:11,250
She said we'd never
see each other again...

213
00:14:11,517 --> 00:14:13,285
She should at least be doing well.

214
00:14:28,133 --> 00:14:29,501
Byeon U An...

215
00:14:29,835 --> 00:14:33,405
I will hunt you down
no matter what, you snake.

216
00:14:34,473 --> 00:14:36,809
That money meant so much!

217
00:14:44,683 --> 00:14:46,135
(Share Waiver and Transfer Agreement)

218
00:14:46,218 --> 00:14:47,603
(Transferors, No Yeong Ju,
Cha Seung Hyun, Cha Seung Woo)

219
00:14:47,686 --> 00:14:49,021
(Transferee, Na Se Ri)

220
00:15:03,068 --> 00:15:04,370
That's refreshing.

221
00:15:04,737 --> 00:15:08,340
Making banh xeo all day was so hot.

222
00:15:09,508 --> 00:15:11,176
Good work, Mai.

223
00:15:11,744 --> 00:15:13,479
It was for a happy occasion.

224
00:15:14,013 --> 00:15:18,684
O Reum! No matter how hard it gets,
I'm so happy.

225
00:15:19,785 --> 00:15:22,321
Thank you for coming home again.

226
00:15:22,988 --> 00:15:24,290
Isn't he beautiful?

227
00:15:24,423 --> 00:15:27,326
Of course! Even more so.

228
00:15:28,527 --> 00:15:32,364
No one else looks this beautiful
with a shaved head.

229
00:15:33,332 --> 00:15:34,967
That's right.

230
00:15:35,067 --> 00:15:40,139
From now on, my O Reum just needs
to grow up healthy, all right?

231
00:15:47,947 --> 00:15:49,682
Hello, this is Cha Seung Woo.

232
00:15:50,282 --> 00:15:53,836
There's trouble at your father's company.

233
00:15:53,919 --> 00:15:56,188
Could you come over here now?

234
00:15:56,588 --> 00:15:58,207
I have no one to talk this over with.

235
00:15:58,290 --> 00:16:00,926
I'm busy right now. What is it?

236
00:16:01,560 --> 00:16:03,495
The truth is...

237
00:16:04,129 --> 00:16:07,199
The lawyer ran off with everything.

238
00:16:07,833 --> 00:16:09,501
What do you mean?

239
00:16:09,969 --> 00:16:13,405
He took off with all my investment!

240
00:16:14,506 --> 00:16:16,241
What am I supposed to do?

241
00:16:16,442 --> 00:16:18,677
Isn't there some way to fix this?

242
00:16:21,580 --> 00:16:22,748
Yes.

243
00:16:23,382 --> 00:16:24,516
Yes.

244
00:16:24,683 --> 00:16:25,918
Thank you.

245
00:16:45,270 --> 00:16:47,573
What's wrong? What happened?

246
00:16:48,240 --> 00:16:50,943
Mai, I'm heading out for a bit.

247
00:16:51,510 --> 00:16:53,779
Who was on the phone?

248
00:16:54,446 --> 00:16:57,683
- That other family.
- Why? Something happened to Ji Ni?

249
00:16:58,083 --> 00:16:59,651
I'll tell you when I'm back.

250
00:17:10,396 --> 00:17:13,749
I wanted to sort the documents,
but I don't really understand them,

251
00:17:13,832 --> 00:17:15,701
so I just put them all together.

252
00:17:16,035 --> 00:17:17,887
I went through them,
so they're all a mess.

253
00:17:17,970 --> 00:17:19,938
You can't even read documents...

254
00:17:20,406 --> 00:17:22,074
and you went into business?

255
00:17:23,108 --> 00:17:26,128
He was the lawyer my husband trusted,
so I trusted him too.

256
00:17:26,211 --> 00:17:28,180
Scams are always run by people you know.

257
00:17:28,447 --> 00:17:30,382
Strangers can't scam you.

258
00:17:30,482 --> 00:17:32,951
Don't scold me. Today has been awful.

259
00:17:37,256 --> 00:17:38,557
But...

260
00:17:38,957 --> 00:17:40,826
Was I really scammed?

261
00:17:41,060 --> 00:17:42,294
Are you certain?

262
00:17:43,228 --> 00:17:44,897
I still can't believe it.

263
00:17:45,130 --> 00:17:46,082
Well...

264
00:17:46,165 --> 00:17:48,100
Go back home and rest for now.

265
00:17:48,333 --> 00:17:50,169
I'll go through everything carefully.

266
00:17:50,836 --> 00:17:51,937
Should I?

267
00:17:52,071 --> 00:17:55,407
Actually, I haven't slept a wink
since yesterday.

268
00:17:55,541 --> 00:17:56,708
Understood.

269
00:18:01,146 --> 00:18:02,948
Hello. Did you find anything out?

270
00:18:03,348 --> 00:18:04,567
Regarding Indonesia.

271
00:18:04,650 --> 00:18:05,818
Yes.

272
00:18:07,086 --> 00:18:08,253
Yes.

273
00:18:10,456 --> 00:18:11,723
I see.

274
00:18:12,191 --> 00:18:13,559
Understood.

275
00:18:14,660 --> 00:18:17,529
- The lawyer's name?
- Byeon U An.

276
00:18:18,363 --> 00:18:20,566
- Byeon U An.
- His name is Byeon U An.

277
00:18:21,333 --> 00:18:23,135
The company is Cha Production.

278
00:18:24,303 --> 00:18:26,105
Yes, the same Cha family name.

279
00:18:26,438 --> 00:18:28,574
It has nothing to do with me.

280
00:18:29,208 --> 00:18:30,509
Yes.

281
00:18:35,347 --> 00:18:38,501
Let's file a police report first.

282
00:18:38,584 --> 00:18:40,953
That Byeon U An, the lawyer...

283
00:18:41,353 --> 00:18:42,521
What a name.

284
00:18:42,621 --> 00:18:44,056
We need to find him first.

285
00:18:44,289 --> 00:18:46,024
And whether his family is gone too.

286
00:18:47,459 --> 00:18:49,928
Indonesia, Dubai, South America,

287
00:18:50,129 --> 00:18:54,366
there are plenty of people running scams
claiming to import Korean content.

288
00:18:54,800 --> 00:18:56,835
The Korean wave makes it easy.

289
00:18:57,703 --> 00:19:00,339
Here they scam you
with shell companies like this,

290
00:19:00,506 --> 00:19:04,109
but in South America and elsewhere,
they raise money promising Korean actors,

291
00:19:04,209 --> 00:19:05,577
and then disappear.

292
00:19:06,078 --> 00:19:08,898
So was my husband deceived from the start?

293
00:19:08,981 --> 00:19:12,784
Back then, the company
may have actually existed.

294
00:19:13,051 --> 00:19:14,753
But after he passed away...

295
00:19:15,888 --> 00:19:18,490
you took over, and you were green...

296
00:19:18,757 --> 00:19:20,859
so he may have changed his mind.

297
00:19:21,326 --> 00:19:23,662
I even flew to Indonesia.

298
00:19:23,795 --> 00:19:25,648
I met everyone involved.

299
00:19:25,731 --> 00:19:27,666
I could fake that much myself.

300
00:19:27,833 --> 00:19:30,035
All it takes is casting a few extras.

301
00:19:31,937 --> 00:19:33,805
I was blind with my eyes wide open.

302
00:19:34,106 --> 00:19:37,309
Anyway, go back home for now.

303
00:19:37,809 --> 00:19:39,745
Even the best make mistakes,

304
00:19:39,945 --> 00:19:42,147
so he may have left a weak spot somewhere.

305
00:19:42,548 --> 00:19:43,949
I'll try to find it.

306
00:19:44,816 --> 00:19:46,285
All right. Thank you.

307
00:19:48,187 --> 00:19:49,288
It's not...

308
00:19:49,821 --> 00:19:51,323
It's too soon to thank me.

309
00:19:51,723 --> 00:19:52,891
I haven't found anything.

310
00:19:52,991 --> 00:19:54,293
I said I'd look.

311
00:19:55,260 --> 00:19:57,729
You can't work if you're this emotional.

312
00:20:32,164 --> 00:20:33,966
Can't focus on work?

313
00:20:37,402 --> 00:20:39,605
I'll go get some air.

314
00:20:48,714 --> 00:20:51,583
It must be hard for her,
not being able to show it.

315
00:21:11,536 --> 00:21:12,971
Yes, it's me.

316
00:21:13,705 --> 00:21:14,873
Right now?

317
00:21:15,007 --> 00:21:16,675
I'm going through the documents.

318
00:21:17,876 --> 00:21:19,678
Your mom went home,

319
00:21:20,045 --> 00:21:21,546
so look after her.

320
00:21:23,282 --> 00:21:25,083
Yes, thank you.

321
00:21:25,384 --> 00:21:26,885
I was with O Reum,

322
00:21:27,052 --> 00:21:28,754
and your mom called me, so I came out.

323
00:21:28,954 --> 00:21:30,255
My O Reum...

324
00:21:31,523 --> 00:21:33,125
You're the one who made it possible
for him to come home.

325
00:21:33,659 --> 00:21:35,227
Mai says it every chance she gets.

326
00:21:35,394 --> 00:21:36,828
"Be good to Ji Ni."

327
00:21:38,664 --> 00:21:40,465
We should help each other where we can.

328
00:21:42,067 --> 00:21:43,402
Yes.

329
00:21:45,537 --> 00:21:47,072
Speak up a little.

330
00:21:47,372 --> 00:21:49,074
You'll collapse before she does.

331
00:21:51,710 --> 00:21:55,113
Who'd have thought I'd be here,
in that man's company.

332
00:21:56,281 --> 00:21:58,050
You really never know what'll happen...

333
00:21:59,818 --> 00:22:01,520
I called because I thought of you,

334
00:22:01,953 --> 00:22:03,522
so forget it all and go home.

335
00:22:03,989 --> 00:22:05,123
Yes.

336
00:22:06,058 --> 00:22:07,359
Yes.

337
00:22:33,051 --> 00:22:34,252
So right now?

338
00:22:35,253 --> 00:22:36,822
I have to go to the police station,

339
00:22:37,189 --> 00:22:39,024
but my legs are shaking...

340
00:22:39,691 --> 00:22:42,294
And I can't bring my daughter along...

341
00:22:43,295 --> 00:22:45,397
Could I ask you to come with me?

342
00:22:45,697 --> 00:22:47,332
Yes, I'll go with you.

343
00:22:47,499 --> 00:22:48,884
Please wait a moment.

344
00:22:48,967 --> 00:22:50,435
I'll tidy things up upstairs
and be right back.

345
00:22:50,802 --> 00:22:51,803
Thank you.

346
00:22:52,137 --> 00:22:53,638
And I'm sorry.

347
00:22:54,539 --> 00:22:56,408
It's fine. Of course I should help.

348
00:23:04,549 --> 00:23:06,585
This is lemon tea.

349
00:23:07,452 --> 00:23:09,087
Stay strong, Se Ri.

350
00:23:10,455 --> 00:23:12,257
Yes, thank you.

351
00:23:15,627 --> 00:23:18,630
The tartness wakes me up a bit.

352
00:23:23,001 --> 00:23:26,438
Mother, I'll give you the prettiest
nails at the reunion.

353
00:23:28,106 --> 00:23:30,108
Show us the flashiest ones you have.

354
00:23:33,178 --> 00:23:34,446
How about this one?

355
00:23:35,947 --> 00:23:37,433
Absolutely not!

356
00:23:37,516 --> 00:23:39,117
Is that the best taste you have?

357
00:23:39,518 --> 00:23:40,752
I'm sorry.

358
00:23:41,086 --> 00:23:42,921
I said the flashiest today, right?

359
00:23:43,722 --> 00:23:44,756
Mother!

360
00:23:45,357 --> 00:23:46,691
How about this?

361
00:23:47,459 --> 00:23:48,894
If I wore that one...

362
00:23:49,127 --> 00:23:50,662
your father-in-law would throw me out.

363
00:23:52,130 --> 00:23:54,099
So he's conservative.

364
00:23:54,466 --> 00:23:56,952
Still, Mother, it's a special day,

365
00:23:57,035 --> 00:23:59,204
so shouldn't you go all out?

366
00:23:59,838 --> 00:24:01,907
No, I prefer something simple.

367
00:24:02,140 --> 00:24:04,509
Just do this one, please.

368
00:24:05,076 --> 00:24:07,179
Mother, that's far too plain.

369
00:24:07,312 --> 00:24:09,448
I have one knockout dress.

370
00:24:09,781 --> 00:24:11,850
The nails don't need to be flashy, either.

371
00:24:12,217 --> 00:24:15,020
Really? I want to see it.

372
00:24:15,720 --> 00:24:17,039
Should I come to the reunion too?

373
00:24:17,122 --> 00:24:18,690
What? You?

374
00:24:18,790 --> 00:24:19,791
Why not?

375
00:24:19,891 --> 00:24:22,761
Wouldn't it be better
if I attended as your assistant?

376
00:24:25,597 --> 00:24:26,932
Let me think about it.

377
00:24:30,302 --> 00:24:32,704
I'll just step out to the restroom.

378
00:24:41,379 --> 00:24:43,565
She kept asking me, "When's the reunion?"

379
00:24:43,648 --> 00:24:45,717
and about your schedule, ma'am.

380
00:24:46,384 --> 00:24:49,371
I don't introduce them until the wedding.

381
00:24:49,454 --> 00:24:51,056
That's true.

382
00:24:51,289 --> 00:24:53,124
Do Hee must have been embarrassed.

383
00:24:53,959 --> 00:24:56,945
Ever since that happened,
I just can't warm up to her.

384
00:24:57,028 --> 00:24:59,998
How could she swing a handbag
at my son right in front of me?

385
00:25:00,966 --> 00:25:02,400
So vulgar.

386
00:25:02,834 --> 00:25:05,370
Honestly, if it weren't
for Ambassador Do,

387
00:25:05,604 --> 00:25:06,922
I'd call the whole thing off.

388
00:25:07,005 --> 00:25:10,976
You'll have to endure it so that Ji Hu
gains a solid family by marriage.

389
00:25:12,577 --> 00:25:14,479
I need a nap.

390
00:25:14,880 --> 00:25:16,014
What's for dinner tonight?

391
00:25:16,147 --> 00:25:18,216
The General has dinner plans.

392
00:25:18,550 --> 00:25:19,551
Really?

393
00:25:19,651 --> 00:25:21,419
Then I'll just have a salad.

394
00:25:26,758 --> 00:25:27,759
Son!

395
00:25:28,426 --> 00:25:30,095
- What are you doing?
- Hello.

396
00:25:30,495 --> 00:25:32,297
I came to the Han River to run with Tae O.

397
00:25:33,064 --> 00:25:34,733
I heard you got your nails done
with Do Hee.

398
00:25:36,468 --> 00:25:38,403
I'll probably have dinner with Tae O.

399
00:25:39,204 --> 00:25:40,405
Yes, I understand.

400
00:25:40,705 --> 00:25:41,706
Yes.

401
00:25:43,008 --> 00:25:44,843
What are you doing? Let's run.

402
00:26:06,197 --> 00:26:08,600
- Really?
- Yes.

403
00:26:09,100 --> 00:26:11,887
Even when I told her to leave early,
she said she'd been a burden,

404
00:26:11,970 --> 00:26:13,872
and stayed until the work was done.

405
00:26:15,106 --> 00:26:16,859
I felt so bad for her.

406
00:26:16,942 --> 00:26:18,810
If it goes to trial,
recommend a good lawyer for her.

407
00:26:19,010 --> 00:26:22,047
I was already planning to ask
my father about it tonight.

408
00:26:22,914 --> 00:26:24,950
What kind of business does her mother run?

409
00:26:25,483 --> 00:26:27,118
I don't know the details,

410
00:26:27,218 --> 00:26:29,387
but her late father was a director.

411
00:26:29,888 --> 00:26:32,958
Probably exporting Korean content.

412
00:26:33,191 --> 00:26:35,894
- Didn't her mother only play cello?
- Exactly.

413
00:26:36,061 --> 00:26:39,030
Ji Ni was against it. She said
they should hire a professional manager.

414
00:26:39,331 --> 00:26:40,765
She should have listened.

415
00:26:42,033 --> 00:26:43,835
What good is regret now?

416
00:26:50,642 --> 00:26:51,876
The house?

417
00:26:53,945 --> 00:26:56,915
You bet the house on it? Behind my back?

418
00:26:57,449 --> 00:27:00,385
That's why I could die in peace.

419
00:27:00,885 --> 00:27:03,722
- I thought you'd be fine without me.
- Mom!

420
00:27:04,889 --> 00:27:06,491
I'm sorry.

421
00:27:07,492 --> 00:27:09,227
This is unbelievable.

422
00:27:10,228 --> 00:27:11,830
Mom, have you always been this reckless?

423
00:27:13,098 --> 00:27:15,900
I wanted to leave every single day.

424
00:27:16,835 --> 00:27:19,704
I didn't want to live
in a world without your dad.

425
00:27:20,005 --> 00:27:21,272
I just...

426
00:27:21,406 --> 00:27:23,875
I thought if I could leave you
with nothing to worry about,

427
00:27:24,109 --> 00:27:25,577
that would be enough.

428
00:27:31,249 --> 00:27:32,917
What do we do?

429
00:27:35,353 --> 00:27:36,721
Do we...

430
00:27:37,756 --> 00:27:39,457
Do we have to move?

431
00:27:40,392 --> 00:27:42,160
Even if they catch Byeon,

432
00:27:42,460 --> 00:27:44,829
it's useless if the money is gone.

433
00:27:45,130 --> 00:27:48,500
Police say he may have gambled it away.

434
00:27:50,268 --> 00:27:53,422
Ms. Kim offered to let us stay
in her studio apartment.

435
00:27:53,505 --> 00:27:55,473
- It would do for now...
- Right away?

436
00:27:56,975 --> 00:27:58,877
The interest is over 10,000 dollars,

437
00:27:59,010 --> 00:28:00,445
and there's nothing left
in the account...

438
00:28:01,312 --> 00:28:02,514
Mom!

439
00:28:02,647 --> 00:28:04,716
What on earth have you done?

440
00:28:29,774 --> 00:28:32,928
(Family Register)

441
00:28:33,011 --> 00:28:36,131
They say whoever makes others cry
ends up shedding tears of blood.

442
00:28:36,214 --> 00:28:37,799
There's nothing more I can do for you,

443
00:28:37,882 --> 00:28:39,334
so file for closure and wind it down.

444
00:28:39,417 --> 00:28:41,470
Maybe I'll remarry
someone worth showing off,

445
00:28:41,553 --> 00:28:44,172
and play the devoted widow
who saves my late husband's company.

446
00:28:44,255 --> 00:28:46,174
Her husband probably died young.

447
00:28:46,257 --> 00:28:49,344
Not true. I heard he had an affair
with some woman who played violin.

448
00:28:49,427 --> 00:28:52,214
Na Ji Ni, how dare someone like you
talk to Ji Hu?

449
00:28:52,297 --> 00:28:55,066
I've put up with you for far too long
for Ji Hu's sake.

450
00:28:57,368 --> 00:28:59,337
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
